Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] retain E900 internal PHY during suspend for WOL

The legacy GXL network setup consumes wol, not G12A's mac_wol property.
internal_phy_suspend() preserves PHY power when this flag is set. This does
not prove shutdown/BL301 wake support; physical suspend/wake remains pending.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/coreelec-gxl/gxlx2_p291_1g_e900v21c.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/coreelec-gxl/gxlx2_p291_1g_e900v21c.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/coreelec-gxl/gxlx2_p291_1g_e900v21c.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/coreelec-gxl/gxlx2_p291_1g_e900v21c.dts
@@ -90,6 +90,8 @@
 
 &ethmac {
 	internal_phy = <1>;
+	/* Legacy internal_phy_suspend keeps power for Magic Packet wake. */
+	wol = <1>;
 	phy-mode = "rmii";
 	mc_val_internal_phy = <0x1800>;
 	/* No external PHY reset or strap GPIOs on this board. */
